**Finding: Missing (critical) — no IP/data ownership provision**

The Site Development and Hosting Agreement has no intellectual property clause at all. HDI designs, develops, hosts and operates the Site and receives all of our Content, Marks and user information, and the parties swap customer e-mail lists under Section 7.1 — but nothing says who owns the Site deliverables, the Content or the customer and order data generated through the Site. Section 10.2's "co-ownership" language addresses only the corporate relationship, not IP.

**Redline (validated, preferred level):** new Section 5.5 inserted after p0035, providing that:
- The Company owns Content, Marks, Deerskin Products materials and all Site deliverables/work product created for it, with HDI assigning any interest;
- HDI retains its pre-existing platform, software and administration tools, but grants a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free, transferable licence to any HDI IP embedded in or needed to use the deliverables;
- All Site customer, user, order and transaction data (including e-mail lists) is exclusively the Company's, usable by HDI only to perform, with a copy returned on request and at termination;
- No joint ownership is created.

Fallback offered in the comment: licence-back to the Site deliverables instead of assignment, provided our ownership of Content and customer data remains unqualified.
